-- ============================================================================
-- DR5 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Geomechanics, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: the mud weight window walked along a whole trajectory,
-- 30 m of measured depth at a time, with the profile interpolated onto each
-- station's true vertical depth. 99 rows on the slant well and 92 on the
-- horizontal one, both checked against the published oracle.
--
-- THE FIRST FINDING. The tightest point is at TOTAL DEPTH on the slant well
-- and at the KICK-OFF POINT on the horizontal one, 1020 m into a 2800 m hole,
-- with the hole barely 5.333333333333236 degrees off vertical. The collapse
-- gradient falls all the way through that interval as the rock strengthens,
-- and the deviation below the kick-off WIDENS the window rather than narrowing
-- it, so the minimum sits where the two trends cross. The hardest place to
-- drill that well is nowhere near the reservoir, and a study that evaluated
-- total depth on both wells would have got one of them right by accident.
--
-- THE SECOND FINDING, WHICH REORDERS EVERYTHING ELSE. The slant well is PORE
-- PRESSURE bound at its tightest point, by 773.5521036358621 kg/m3. The
-- horizontal well is COLLAPSE bound at its, by 333.0134212003486. Which bound
-- binds decides the remedy, the uncertainty, the failure mode AND which
-- parameters matter: sweeping the friction angle from 20 to 40 degrees moves
-- the slant well's window by EXACTLY ZERO at every digit, because neither of
-- its two bounds contains a friction angle, while it moves the horizontal
-- well's by 216.4400735919205 kg/m3.
--
-- THE THIRD FINDING. The Poisson ratio dominates every other sensitivity.
-- Sweeping it from 0.20 to 0.35, which is this course's OWN sandstone-to-shale
-- seed range, moves the slant well's window by 956.2616032453875 kg/m3 and the
-- horizontal well's by 1153.222084676116. The next largest are the SHmax
-- azimuth at 366.7313503391106 on the slant well and the tensile strength at
-- 496.6885864429339 on the horizontal one. So the parameter with the largest
-- influence is the one usually taken from a lithology table, and on this
-- evidence a dipole shear sonic beats core and an extended leak-off test as
-- the first thing to buy. That contradicts the conventional wish list, and the
-- general lesson is that the ranking should be COMPUTED rather than assumed.
--
-- FIVE THINGS TAUGHT IN m05 AND CERTIFIED NOWHERE: inelastic and anisotropic
-- rock behaviour, time-dependent effects, chemical effects, thermal stress,
-- and natural fractures and bedding.
-- 20260830_dr5_geomech_go_live.sql asserts that no graded field key names one.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

